# Testing Guidelines

This file contains test guidelines for Cursor IDE, focusing on Docker container verification.

## Core Principles

1. Follow the [Better Specs](https://www.betterspecs.org/) guidelines whenever possible
2. Prefer BDD/Gherkin approach for writing test specifications
3. Use table-driven tests to reduce code duplication and improve readability
4. Keep tests minimal, focused, and documented

## Testing Frameworks

### Container Testing

- [Container-Structure-Test](https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/container-structure-test) is the primary framework for verifying Docker containers
- Define tests that validate:
  - File existence and permissions
  - Command outputs
  - Container metadata
  - Environment variables

### Language-Specific Testing

- **Lua**: Use [Busted](https://lunarmodules.github.io/busted/) for automated testing
- **Shell**: Use [shellspec](https://shellspec.info) for shell script testing
- **Makefiles**: Use [shellspec](https://shellspec.info) for verifying Makefile targets

### Integration Testing

- [Testcontainers](https://testcontainers.com) for advanced container integration testing scenarios

## Documentation Requirements

1. Document any special setup or requirements for tests
2. Include example test cases where possible
3. Provide clear failure messages that aid in debugging
